  "findings": [],
  "review": {
    "workflows": "All nine invoked workflows have explicit input tables, fixed accepted roles and exact profile/output caps. Prepared rows bind kind/ID/path/format/expected hash; configured roots and manifests do not enlarge grants.",
    "authority": "The six-key root prepare, exact resolver deployment, native start, granted operations, agent-output finalization with non-null invocation and empty inputs, native stop and explicit root result are ordered. Missing configuration blocks except root bootstrap; missing native capability never falls back to local-user authority.",
    "role_precision": "Non-reviewer reports are restricted to the exact output manifest. Reconciler-derived acceptance does not authorize feature-contract writes. Source facts, unknown expectations, implementation evidence, incremental structural validity and completion authority remain distinct; valid reviewer FAIL is output-valid/result-fail.",
    "root_operations": "Initialization/configuration and approval are separate root-only operations. The reviewer receives only exact reports after valid projected/resulting context. Decision proposals do not approve/reject/supersede history; separate root approval requires owner, explicit evidence, current expected hash and fresh later validation.",
    "aliases": "Seven aliases dispatch directly to closed canonical targets with no independent tools, outputs, scheduler or business rules. Umbrella skill_id and coverage action=inventory|extract|review are human authoring selectors, not extra service wire fields. Parity ownership is Requirements Reconciler; review never grants ledger writes.",
    "test_contract": "The 467-line test module uses checked-in static fixtures only and asserts closed metadata/input/output maps, accepted-role subsets, lifecycle ordering, denial/memory/freshness rules, all role-specific distinctions and exact alias dispatch. The corrected initializer literal preserves the actual frozen no-configuration-write boundary."
  },
